# Shell scripts keep LF on every checkout, Windows included.
#
# This repo is cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF in the working tree. That is fine for the C# sources, but build.sh
# is run through WSL, and a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "bash\r":
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# The index already stores LF, so this only changes what lands on disk.
*.sh text eol=lf
